{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat any abominable thing.</b> Before the giving of the Torah, the distinction between impure and pure was already known, as is explained in the matter of Noah (Genesis 7:2). In any event, when the blessed El permitted Noah and his sons to eat living creatures, He did not distinguish between impure and pure. You, however, being holy, it is not fitting for you to be nourished from the impure and the abominable, so that you not resemble its temperament."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:25.280936665Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}